      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum daily dose:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nAt this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the 2,550 mg/day maximum, and 1700 may be a typo for 850.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** For example, 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with your rationale. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
      }
     ],
